WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — mei (90s) Narrator Nylo

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.061
First, give a computer a fixed energy budget upfront,

2
00:00:04.061 --> 00:00:07.025
and get the best answer inside that limit.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:10.817
Second, a tiny food tag can refuse routine

4
00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:15.285
radio chatter in freezing cargo so safety alerts survive.

5
00:00:15.785 --> 00:00:22.694
Third, a data center can obey power-grid caps by pausing flexible work without giving wrong answers.

6
00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:28.839
At room temperature, a ten-microwatt sensing schedule lets a coin battery run roughly

7
00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:36.011
eight years. Inside a minus-twenty-degree freezer truck, internal battery resistance jumps nearly sixfold to

8
00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:41.989
seventy-two ohms, causing unbudgeted wireless bursts to sag below two volts and brown out.

9
00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:48.006
Metabolic Intelligence prices both energy spent and decision error before acting. On the

10
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:54.715
tag, a lightweight binding classifier needs just one thousand seven hundred twenty-three instructions—about

11
00:00:54.715 --> 00:01:02.928
ninety-two nanojoules—while split energy grants protect a dedicated thirty-five-millijoule reserve for critical temperature alarms.

12
00:01:03.428 --> 00:01:09.713
Across ten thousand simulated cold-chain wakeups, refusing four hundred ninety routine beacons

13
00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:15.931
preserved all forty safety alerts without fail. On a modeled hundred-megawatt campus speaking

14
00:01:15.931 --> 00:01:22.148
real grid-signaling protocols, ordered controls plus server sleep held zero minutes over cap.

15
00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:29.629
Complete two-layer circuit board layouts, component tables, and three-dimensional enclosure models ship openly,

16
00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:36.295
with every single figure labeled as datasheet or simulation until physical boards return from fabrication.
